    rules:[
      'The phone number is the identity. A workspace is created from a phone plus a business name; email is optional and used only for reports and receipts. No account may require an email address to exist.',
      'Sign-up creates exactly two records — the Workspace and its owner User — and nothing else. No module is installed, no site is configured, no capability is turned on until the owner asks for it.',
      'Sign-up never verifies anything. No SMS code, no email confirmation, no waiting: the credential is a phone plus a password set on the form, and the workspace is usable the moment it is created. Speed of first sale beats proof of contact.',
      'Verification is a separate, later feature, not a gate. A phone or email carries verified_at (null until proven) and is verified on demand from Settings — or demanded by a specific capability that genuinely needs it (statutory registers, payout accounts, password recovery by SMS). Nothing else in the product may block on an unverified contact.',
      'Every sign-in attempt is recorded with phone, device, result and time, whether it succeeded or failed. Repeated failures rate-limit the phone, never the device, so a shared till cannot be locked out by one operator.',
      'A suspended user authenticates and is refused with a stated reason. Access withdrawal is never presented as a wrong credential.',
      'Language is the operator’s choice, not the tenant’s: EN / FR is switchable on every public screen and persisted on the device (localStorage kz-lang), and it survives sign-up into the authenticated session.',
      'The introduction is always skippable and never a gate. Nothing about it is recorded against the account, and no path may require passing through it to reach sign-up.',
      'Sign-up completed offline is queued with its client-generated id and submits on reconnect; the operator is told the workspace is pending, never that it failed.',
      'One shell, one navigation grammar. Every module — including the ones authored before the shell existed — renders in the same stage: the app fills the surface, the rail is the module’s own screens, and the device is a preview control, never chrome around the product.',
      'A module’s child pages are not modules. Submissions, Builder, Runs, Designer and the Orchestrator belong to their parent and appear in the parent’s rail, so a page and its siblings can never disagree about what exists.',
      'The rail definition for a module lives in exactly one place. A page must not hand-write its own copy of the module’s screen list.',
      'The launcher is a projection of the capability service, not a list of files. A tile whose module is off, or whose capability is hidden, is absent — never present and inert.',
      'Retiring a module from the catalogue enters the same Winding state as a tier change; obligations already made do not disappear because a tile was switched off.',
      'A role may only subtract from the plan and the tier. No grant can hand a tenant a capability their plan does not include.',
      'Suspending a user removes access and keeps every record they created, including the shifts, sales and submissions attributed to them.',
      'Access control and Settings are visible on a phone but editable only where the audit trail can be trusted; every write is stamped with actor, device and time.',
    ],
